##! Please refer to the documentation at
##! https://coreruleset.org/docs/development/regex_assembly/.

##! Rule 944170: Malformed Base64 padding in Authorization credentials (Java4Shell)
##!
##! Sibling of 944160 for `Authorization: <scheme> <credentials>`. The
##! credentials (Base64 or Base64url token of at least 64 characters
##! followed by `=` padding) are captured in TX:1, and the chained rule
##! checks their alignment with `t:length`.
##!
##! The scheme is an RFC 9110 token, followed by one or more spaces.
##!
##! Only single-character repeats are used, no repeated groups. The
##! expression is RE2 compatible.
##!
##! Ref: https://calif.io/java4shell

##!^ ^[A-Za-z][!#$%&'*+.^_`|~0-9A-Za-z\-]* +(
##!$ =+)$

##! Standard alphabet
(?:[A-Za-z0-9+/]{64,})
##! URL-safe alphabet
(?:[A-Za-z0-9_\-]{64,})
